 "equipment_type": "Pump system controller (variable speed, differential pressure)",
 "applies_to": "Tigerflow packaged variable-speed pump systems run by the Mark VI controller with up to three VFD pumps and zone differential pressure sensors.",
 "summary": "The Mark VI controls up to three VFD pumps on zone differential pressure. Over BACnet it reports pump run commands, VFD run and fault feedback, HOA positions, zone differential pressures, flow, pump speeds and supply/return temperatures. The BMS can write a system disable (BV 41) and a differential pressure setpoint for zones 1-3 (AV 41-43).",
 "bacnet_transport": [],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Instance plan differs from the Mark V list; do not reuse a Mark V map.",
  "Instances are printed as BV0001.. / AV0001.. with gaps that are not in the list.",
  "The list has four zone pressure sensor failure flags but only three zone pressure readings and three BAS zone setpoints.",
  "The point list does not state the BACnet transport (IP or MS/TP) or device addressing.",
  "Units as printed: pressure psi, flow GPM, temperatures °F."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "MARK VI - BACNet POINT LIST",
